From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaozhi mpv build <build@local.invalid>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 23:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ao_wasapi: preserve representable height channel layouts

WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE can describe layouts such as 5.1.4 and 7.1.4 with
its 32-bit channel mask.  Do not reduce every layout above eight channels
to 7.1 before IAudioClient::IsFormatSupported gets a chance to probe it.

The shared-mode path already falls back to the device mix format when an
exact layout is rejected, while the exclusive-mode path already searches
the standard layouts.  Keep the old fallback only for channel maps which
cannot be represented by the WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE DWORD mask.
---
 audio/out/ao_wasapi_utils.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/audio/out/ao_wasapi_utils.c b/audio/out/ao_wasapi_utils.c
index a1e116b6c..b8a7f40f0 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_wasapi_utils.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_wasapi_utils.c
@@ -203,11 +203,10 @@ static void set_waveformat(WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE *wformat,
 
     uint64_t chans = mp_chmap_to_waveext(channels);
     wformat->dwChannelMask = chans;
 
-    if (wformat->Format.nChannels > 8 || wformat->dwChannelMask != chans) {
-        // IAudioClient::IsFormatSupported tend to fallback to stereo for closest
-        // format match when there are more channels. Remix to standard layout.
-        // Also if input channel mask has channels outside 32-bits override it
+    if (wformat->dwChannelMask != chans) {
+        // If the input channel mask has channels outside 32 bits, override it
         // and hope for the best...
+        // Representable layouts above 8 channels are probed as-is.
         wformat->dwChannelMask = KSAUDIO_SPEAKER_7POINT1_SURROUND;
         wformat->Format.nChannels = 8;
     }
